\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
The Standard Model of particle physics and General Relativity are fundamentally challenged by two fine-tuning dilemmas: the origin of the nineteen flavor parameters (fermion mass hierarchies, CKM/PMNS mixing angles, and CP-violating phases) and the $10^{120}$ discrepancy between quantum zero-point vacuum energy and the observed cosmological dark energy density ($\Lambda$). In this paper, we show that both problems find a geometric resolution within continuous simplicial geometry on $\Delta_4 \times \Delta_2$.
First, the $S_3$ permutation symmetry of the boundary 2-simplex $\Delta_2$ decomposes the mass root vector via $\R^3 \cong \mathbf{1} \oplus \mathbf{2}$; the circulant orbit condition imposes norm equipartition $\|\mathbf{v}_{\mathbf{2}}\|^2 = \|\mathbf{v}_{\mathbf{1}}\|^2$, establishing identically three generations, the exact charged lepton Koide ratio $Q_l = 2/3$, and a two-parameter family $(v_0, \delta_l)$ yielding $m_\tau \approx 1776.88\text{ MeV}$ ($0.012\sigma$ PDG).
Second, holographic anyonic braiding ($B_3 \to S_3$) dynamically freezes a complex topological phase during 3D percolation, generating the Kobayashi--Maskawa CP-violating phase $\delta_{\mathrm{CP}}$ and Jarlskog invariant $J_{\mathrm{CP}} \approx 3.08 \times 10^{-5}$.
Third, the QCD radiative correction at the electroweak scale phenomenologically shifts the quark Koide ratio to $Q_q \approx \frac{2}{3}(1 + \alpha_s/\sqrt{3}) \approx 0.712$, while barycentric centroid projection derives the Cabibbo angle $\sin \theta_C \approx 0.2265$.
Fourth, the inter-dimensional fractional trace transform $\mathcal{R}_{3 \to 1}^\alpha$ scales color-singlet neutrino masses down to $m_\nu \sim v_{\EW}^2 / M_{\GUT} \approx 0.03\text{ eV}$ with large PMNS mixing angles ($\sin^2 \theta_{12} \approx 1/3, \sin^2 \theta_{23} \approx 1/2$).
Finally, on the spacetime 4-simplex $\Delta_4$, the Simplicial Euler--Maclaurin face defect recurrence causes the leading quartic ($M_P^4$) and quadratic ($M_P^2 m^2$) zero-point divergences to cancel identically (topological, exact). The residual vacuum energy density is governed by the Barnes $G$-function logarithmic entropy defect density $\mathcal{E}_\infty = \ln 2 - 1/2$ and the effective coupling $\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}} \approx 0.115$, yielding $\rho_\Lambda = M_P^4 e^{-2\pi / (\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}\mathcal{E}_\infty)} \sim 10^{-122} M_P^4 \approx (2.28\text{ meV})^4$, in agreement with cosmological observations. The quartic cancellation is unconditional; the exponential residual is a calibrated qualitative mechanism.
\end{abstract}

