% ==============================================================================
\section{Introduction and Dual Hierarchy Puzzles}
% ==============================================================================

Modern theoretical physics faces two monumental fine-tuning puzzles:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{The Flavor Hierarchy Problem}: The nineteen free parameters of the Standard Model (fermion masses ranging from $m_\nu \sim 10^{-3}\text{ eV}$ to $m_t \approx 173\text{ GeV}$, CKM/PMNS mixing angles, and CP-violating phases) lack a foundational geometric explanation \cite{weinberg1967model,kobayashi1973cp,koide1983fermion}.
    \item \textbf{The Cosmological Constant Problem}: Quantum Field Theory predicts a vacuum zero-point energy density $\rho_{\mathrm{vac}} \sim M_{\Pl}^4 \approx 10^{74}\text{ GeV}^4$, which is $10^{120}$ orders of magnitude larger than the observed dark energy density $\rho_\Lambda \approx 2.7 \times 10^{-47}\text{ GeV}^4$ \cite{weinberg1989cosmological,planck2018}.
\end{enumerate}

In this paper, we show that both puzzles are fundamentally solved by the \textbf{Non-Perturbative Geometric Invariants} of continuous simplicial boundaries $\Delta_m$.

