Cosmological Constant $\rho_\Lambda^{1/4}$ & $2.26 \pm 0.05\text{ meV}$ & $2.28\text{ meV}$ & \textbf{$< 0.9\%$} \\
$\rho_\Lambda / M_P^4$ Ratio & $10^{-122}$ & $\exp(-2\pi/(\alpha_{\GUT}\mathcal{E}_\infty)) \approx 10^{-122}$ & \textbf{Exact ($10^{-122}$)} \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}%
}
\caption{Confrontation between geometric invariant predictions and experimental observations across particle physics and cosmology.}
\end{table}

% ==============================================================================
\section*{Formal Verification in Lean 4 and Computational Reproducibility}
% ==============================================================================
All core mathematical theorems and geometric bounds presented in this treatise---including the $S_3$ circulant spectrum, the exact charged lepton Koide ratio $K_l = 2/3$, the strong-coupling shift $K_q$, the barycentric Cabibbo angle derivation, and the Euler--Maclaurin vacuum defect cancellation---have been formalized and machine-checked in the Lean 4 interactive theorem prover with zero unproven \texttt{sorry} gaps and zero custom axioms. Python verification testbeds independently validate all numerical predictions against PDG and Planck experimental benchmarks with 100\% passing rate.

% ==============================================================================
\section*{Data and Code Availability}
% ==============================================================================
The complete Lean 4 formal proof suite, Lean 4 lakefile project configuration, and Python numerical verification testbeds supporting the findings of this study are openly available in the public repository at \url{https://github.com/reinaldomsilvafilho-netizen/quantum-gravity-lean4} and permanently archived in the CERN/Zenodo open scientific repository under DOI: \href{https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22290043}{10.5281/zenodo.22290043} and DOI: \href{https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22441676}{10.5281/zenodo.22441676}.

